Dispute resolution process:
If the Trust receives an invoice which it reasonably believes includes a sum which is not valid and properly due or any other inaccuracy which renders the invoice invalid (a "disputed invoice");

notify the supplier/ contractor in writing as soon as reasonably practicable;

to the extent the disputed element is readily identifiable, the Customer shall pay any element of the disputed invoice which is not in dispute by its due date;

once the dispute has been resolved, where either Party is required to make a balancing payment, it shall do so within 5 working days and, where the Contractor is required to issue a credit note and/ or fresh invoice, it shall do so within 5 working days.

We would contact the supplier as soon as possible to try to obtain a satisfactory conclusion and to settle any outstanding debt.
The main reasons for any late payments are:
• Original invoice not being received;
• Invoice disputed;
• Invoice date in advance of service and hence payment deliberately delayed (with appropriate communication to supplier);
• Overall credit balances e.g. exam bodies; and
• Occasionally workload/holiday closures mean invoices are not processed as quickly at Academies.

